      "rationale": "Fuel is the largest single operating cost for trucking firms; a deferred and potentially forgiven $0.244/gal tax directly supports Q4 margins."
    },
    {
      "name": "Agriculture & Farm Equipment",
      "impact": "tailwind",
      "rationale": "Dyed diesel penalty waiver plus tax deferral lowers input costs for planting, harvesting, and irrigation operations."
    },
    {
      "name": "Fuel Distribution & Retail",
      "impact": "tailwind",
      "rationale": "Penalty relief on dyed diesel sales for highway use reduces compliance costs and expands legal sales flexibility for distributors."
    },
    {
      "name": "Refiners & Integrated Oils",
      "impact": "headwind",
      "rationale": "A lower effective tax on diesel consumer prices could marginally compress crack spreads at the margin, though volumes are unaffected."
    }
  ],
